          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "[carried from the 91ab26c39d review, code unchanged by 88720eec64, b47e216668 and e7cff40986] default_base picks the highest vX.Y.Z tag that does NOT contain HEAD, not the nearest ancestor release. Measured on the real tag set with the helper's own pipeline (git tag replaced by the equivalent git for-each-ref --no-contains, since this lane may not run git tag): for this PR head it returns v0.69.3, which is NOT an ancestor of HEAD (merge-base --is-ancestor rc=1; 701 commits of v0.69.3 are not on HEAD's line); the nearest ancestor release tag of HEAD is v0.69.0. Same on origin/release/pv-0.69.2 (v0.69.3, rc=1). So on main the default comparison is against a release-branch tree, and the FAIL message 'definitions added between <base> and <head>' is not literally true."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/cb200_head_vs_base.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 84
